From: mscharged-port
Subject: Tweak: a training match's pause has TRAINING OPTIONS
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

A training match (g_bTrainingMatch, offline: the launcher's, or Strikers
101's FREE PLAY, tweak patch 0092) has no use for the pause menu's
Statistics. Its button is now TRAINING OPTIONS, as a challenge's is its
objectives: the host's text (mscharged_tweak_training_options_text, the
module's English without one) on the button's three slides, set when the
scene is created. Its press goes to the host
(mscharged_tweak_menu_press_taken, as Audio and Visual Options do with
Recharged's menus on), whose training page opens over the menu, which stays
as it is; with nothing to take it, the Statistics come as before.

The team that trains gets its item at every kickoff when it holds none
(cGame's kickoff reset), and keeps it when using it (DesireUsePowerup), so
another item from the page would never come. The kickoff's code is now
GiveTrainingItem, which the host's page also calls (through its menu
command, in the game's next frame) with `replace`: what the team holds goes
(ClearAllPowerUps, ClearCurrentPowerUp; one already thrown plays on), and
the new item comes in its place, none for none.

